    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13187" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-plĕo</span></b> , ēvi,
			2, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v.
				a., to empty out, to draw off</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato R.
					R. 64 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 12, 50, 8</span></i>, and 10: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanguinem,</span>”
				<i>to let blood, to bleed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 16, 43, § 148</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">for which, d. animal,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. A. V. 1, 13, 4</span></i>
			.— <b>Poet.</b>, <i>to
				exhaust</i>, haustu fontes, <i><span class="en">Stat. Ach. 1,
				8</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitam querelis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Manil. 4, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
